  "scope_id": "TRIPLE-SYSTEM-20261027-001",
  "title": "At r = 2 the Lie triple system decides: counting maps to nilpotent-by-involution groups is polynomial iff it is abelian",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "For p-groups of exponent p with an involution, counting maps from closed 3-manifold groups with H1(M; F_p) = 0 is polynomial whenever the Lie triple system of the minus part is abelian, in every class, since every homomorphism then lies in a class-2 subgroup; and for graded algebras of class at most 4 it is #P-hard otherwise, already on 2-surgeries of knots. So at r = 2 brackets of two minus elements never matter and brackets of three decide.",
  "authority_class": "proof",
